                    "QualificationSummary": "Your resume must also demonstrate at least one year of Specialized experience at or equivalent to the (GS-11/12, DP-03) grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: Providing technical direction to contractors and other organizations on the development and integration of the software capabilities. Incumbent will serve as the government expert on system interface and software architecture. Using and troubleshooting of simulators, test tools, software toolchains, and software version control systems. Generating and providing input to documentation associated with program organization, product development, system requirements, and technical reports. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website: Electrical Engineering Series 0850 (opm.gov) Computer Engineering Series 0854 (opm.gov) Electronics Engineering Series 0855 (opm.gov) Computer Science Series 1550 (opm.gov) Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.",
