                    ],
                    "QualificationSummary": "One year of specialized experience equivalent in level of difficulty and responsibility to that of the next lower grade within the federal service, which demonstrates the ability to perform the duties of the position, is required. Specialized Experience for the GS-07 is defined as: assisting office and management personnel by gathering, consolidating, and analyzing various types of information, and utilizing regulations and instructions to answer questions and remedy standard issues identified by organizational leadership or management. Specialized Experience for the GS-09 is defined as: applying knowledge of the rules, procedures, operations, organization, and functions of an organization sufficient to perform all administrative support work of the office of a Senior Leader or department head. Examples of Specialized Experience for the GS-09: Managing and scheduling appointments; using office automation software; researching, interpreting and applying clerical and administrative regulations, reviewing correspondence to ensure compliance with regulations, grammar, format and special policies for correspondence are followed; advising action officers in subordinate units on such matters as the application of procedures, correspondence and reporting requirements; maintaining appointment calendars, scheduling conferences/meetings, maintaining files, and making travel arrangements; greeting and interacting with visitors to the Senior Leader. Paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., Peace Corps, AmeriCorps) and other organizations (e.g., professional; philanthropic; religious; spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates to paid employment. You will receive credit for all qualifying experience.",
                    "PositionRemuneration": [
