                    "QualificationSummary": "Mandatory Requirements: Expert knowledge and understanding of Federal and IC budget policies, authorizations, and appropriations processes and procedures. Demonstrated success in presenting and defending budget justifications to OMB and Congress. Displayed experience of IC financial and business planning processes and ability to formulate, defend, and implement ODNI programs and budgets. Extensive knowledge of analytic, diagnostic, and qualitative techniques sufficient to identify, evaluate, and recommend appropriate solutions to resolve the most complex financial matters. Comprehensive knowledge of the ODNI mission, objectives, policies and current events. Exemplary problem-solving skills and ability to identify problems and implement corrective processes. Displayed experience and skill in communicating, negotiating, and advocating a position or solution involving innovative acquisition management or related programs for a major organization involving internal and external customers. Significant experience leading strategic planning, managing, and directing the successful efforts of a large government or private organization. Desired Requirements: Expert communication and interpersonal skills, including ability to exert influence with senior leadership and communicate effectively at all staff levels, both internal and external to the organization. Familiarity with the full range of civilian personnel policies as used by the federal government.",
